{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/232530-demons-partitioning-memory-and-going-native","id":232530,"title":"Demons, Partitioning Memory and Going Native","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-18T00:17:22-07:00","id":232530,"title":"Demons, Partitioning Memory and Going Native","content":"Hey everyone, Nyx here with an opinion question. I currently run a crossover game, (8 players at the moment) and everyone is starting out as human. This posed a problem, because two of my players really wanted to play as Demons. I gave them my approval, and they asked how I intended to make a human into a Demon. I was at first unsure of an answer, but refused to admit as much, and assuaged their worries with a knowing smile and promise to surprise them. After a lot of thought on this issue, an idea hit me. Much like President Zaphod Beeblebrox, the characters have edited their own memories, hiding their supernatural capabilities and memories from themselves while they live full time in a cover. Now, there are a myriad of reasons they might have desired to do this, but, more important than the why of it is how possible it is to do it.<br /> <br /> So, that brings me to the question(s) at hand: does this sound at least plausible, and, how would you feel/react, as a player, if this was written into your character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T00:28:47-07:00","id":232555,"title":"","content":"I think it's a little weird. Keep in mind that Demons have the fundamental issue of Cover instead of Integrity, in addition to the Conditions/Glitches they might suffer as a result of breaking it. You could represent this by pretending that Cover Breaking Points are Integrity Breaking Points and that the characters might experience Glitches as something very strange and supernatural happening to them.<br /> <br /> Honestly, as to how? I'm sure you could have some kind of suborned Infrastructure that could make a hole in their memories, but um. It just begs the question of why they would do that instead of just being regular old Demons in their Covers.<br /> <br /> Three other issues:<br /> <br /> The whole Liar's Face thing.<br /> Eidetic Memory<br /> Demons speak every living language thing<br /> <br /> So if they're humans who seem to not display emotion unless they deliberately choose to do it, have absolutely perfect recall of whatever fake Amnesiac lives they have, and also happen to be omniglots who seem to understand every living language they come across, perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T01:30:31-07:00","id":232606,"title":"","content":"I believe it's completely plausible so long as it revolves around the Demon's own strange condition. It seems to me that half the reason why your player's want to play as Demons is to inject aspects of the God Machine into your Chronicle, and if you were to have that be not only what ties them to the Chronicle but also responsible for their strange situation then I think you'd be able to reinforce their decision to play as a Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T02:40:30-07:00","id":232627,"title":"","content":"Have the God-Machine have done it to them. For whatever reason it wants to store some Demons for some future use. So it hides them inside a special cover making them think they're just normal humans. It removes any need to mechanically justify the modifications.<br /> <br /> For an added bonus, if you have some prominent NPCs you could have them be angels watching over the prisoners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T04:32:02-07:00","id":232676,"title":"","content":"Do I think turning a Demon human long term is plausible? Eh, not really.<br /> <br /> That said, it's six am and I don't want to go to sleep quite yet, so let's roll with it! Rambling ahead!<br /> <br /> Let's set aside the who and the why for right now and focus on the how, and when it comes to unique stuff related to the God-Machine I almost always fall back on Infrastructure. Whether implemented by the God-Machine or exiles, or suborned by the Unchained themselves, it seems pretty solidly like a very unique sort of Concealment Infrastructure. If it is Infrastructure, a few questions come to mind: what form does it take? Is it linked to any other Infrastructure? What did it take to get it going in the first place and what consequences does that action have nowadays? Does it require any maintenance now, and who does it if so? What's the Linchpin, and how can you or the players take care of it when it comes time for the humans to become Unchained once again? The Infrastructure can be personalized, like an implant, or it could be oddly detached, like a building somewhere in the same city. Maybe it's tied to a section of the city that's under construction, and as more of it's renovated the Infrastructure weakens, allowing for flashes of memory, gaining the Unseen Senses: God-Machine merit temporarily, or other such things. Perhaps once the last building is demolished the Infrastructure shatters, simultaenously releasing the quantum state of their Cover and breaking whatever tracking mechanism They had in place (somewhat mirroring the Fall, actually). The last bit is assuming that the PCs aren't the ones behind it in the first place.<br /> <br /> (Side note: you could probably achieve the implant version as a rare Lambda Gadget that simultaneously keeps them human, wipes their memory and allow those who implanted it to keep track of them. Or you could keep the human and memory effects in one Gadget and the tracking in a different one, allowing the new Demons to have to figure out how They're still finding them, again assuming that the Demons themselves aren't Them, if that makes any sense. All the effects are in published Embeds, so it's not out of the realm of possibility. Remember to chip your pets and rogue demons!)<br /> <br /> Speaking of Them, I think the idea that the PCs were the ones who wanted to become human and lose their memory and did so under their own power...isn't very plausible at all. A few other options that immediately come to mind.<br /> <br /> 1. The God-Machine or other Loyalist forces. Easiest to justify how it's done, strangely hard to explain <i>why</i> it was done instead of the demons being forcibly debriefed and recycled or frozen in a Facility for a rainy day.<br /> <br /> 2. Other Unchained. The idea that the PCs had information that was too damaging to let them roam free but too valuable to discard entirely rings fairly true, and it's not too much of a logical leap to say that an easy way to keep that information in check and completely under the God-Machine's radar is to make them a mindwiped muggle. This opens up the idea of other Unchained &quot;handlers&quot; lurking in the shadows, which is a bonus!<br /> <br /> 3. The PCs, via a deal they made with Exiles. Doesn't make much more sense than if the PCs were able to do it themselves, but marginally more interesting and with potential hooks.<br /> <br /> These are, of course, only options that deal exclusively with the God-Machine. Depending on how crossover heavy your games, there could be entirely different reasons for who, how, and why these Unchained were decommissioned! Most of them aren't possible by canon but hey, this entire exercise is about playing fast and loose with those assumptions. Perhaps they were blessed (or cursed!) by a god of the Shadow, or maybe they made a bargain with one of the True Fae. Maybe the Principle has a plan and via quashilim and Pyros shenanigans the Unchained were forced through a temporary version of the Pilgrimage, or maybe someone dragged them down to that weird ocean in the Underworld and stuck them underwater until both they and reality forgot they were demons! Maybe we break the glass and reach for that always-so-easy answer of &quot;a wizard, er, archmage did it&quot; - why? For who? What was the Quintessence that it took to perform the spell, and what did it cost to get the favor in the first place? Whoever did it, even if it was the PCs, two questions have to be answered: what was so important that they needed to be kept alive while also being contained in a very convoluted manner? If it was the PCs, what was so heinous that their memories and their basic natures had to be changed?<br /> <br /> Okay, that's all for now. Maybe more rambling later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T06:20:45-07:00","id":232781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or frozen in a Facility for a rainy day. </div> </div> </div>That's potentially an answer right there. Nothing says the G-M has to store demons in a supernatural warehouse. It might be equally easy to simply mess with their cover and let them live as mortals until needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T08:18:10-07:00","id":232841,"title":"","content":"...you could just have them each make a soul pact with a demon, who cashes in at an opportune time. Their Cover is still the human, and now they're playing a demon. That was the proposed solution in another thread.<br /> I know it's not ideal and they're not technically playing the same character once that happens, mind you, but it's hackable.<br /> I do like the memory-hole idea; you could just as easily make a certain Infrastructure they take down later in the game be something that re-sets them to &quot;full&quot; demonic power.<br /> <br /> Demons are perfect liars, but not perfect lie detectors; the self-deception of the sleeper agent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T08:41:08-07:00","id":232851,"title":"","content":"I think the partition idea is great and works well thematically. You could work a solid Jason Borne vibe into the whole thing. I also like the idea that the Machine did it to them, but I' probably leave just enough confusion surrounding how they were partitioned to keep it unclear if the G-M did in on purpose. Maybe they are actually the only two survivors of a Ring that hit an infrastructure. Maybe they were still plugged in when the whole place imploded leading to some corrupted memory sectors that cause them to think they are their covers.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T10:13:41-07:00","id":232966,"title":"","content":"Alright, very cool ideas everyone! In the spirit of rousing more conversation, I'll add in more of my setting information. The players set them selves up very close to my G-M plans for this city. One player is playing a psychiatrist/counselor at a high school, moonlighting at an addiction rehabilitation facility. She doesn't know that the facility is indoctrinating everyone inside of it, and those who break under the subliminal messaging are taken into the basement for repurposing.The other player is at a college, which is my most infrastructure heavy location. I have two NPC Demons, a Messenger Saboteur/Inquisitor named Walter Ifi (complete with all the electronic systems and spy software I could combine) and Ms. Sunshine a Destroyer Tempter/Inquisitor (designed to imitate the classical image of an angel with a fire theme).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T04:42:58-07:00","id":236327,"title":"","content":"I can see two more possible explanations by the by.<br /> <br /> The characters were hit with some weird gadget, perhaps a lambda gadget, or perhaps the humans were possessed will be possessed by angels who fall, since what happens when a possessing angel falls has never been made clear, if you want to rule that the human host/demon merge in such a way that effectively the human characters became demons, well that's ST prerogative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T11:17:00-07:00","id":236715,"title":"","content":"Or do it like in my campaign: a mage deleted a huge part of their memories. In this case, they wouldn't remember any of the previous missions, they would have only flashbacks during sleep about a hunted deactivated prision (infrastructure that they were tied up to) and a security guard in there (an angel protecting it)<br /> <br /> <br /> If this crossover could involve a lot of mage's themes, make them hunt the mage or discover why he's done it (probably because the mage was the target that the players were supposed to kill, God-machine hates this humans who wants to alter the reality. It's not safe to have mortals discovering their inner God powers.). This mage can also be a nice contact/ally (or make an angel kill him to add more paranoia and introduce the antagonist. I believe after his death, the magic would fade and they should be able to remember everything)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}